From 0330bddb509a358e556e266739d8761735c8d4d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henry Wang <Henry.Wang@arm.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jun 2022 03:17:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] xen/arm: Apply MPAM config to dom0less domUs

In dom0less systems, it is not usually very easy to use Xentool to
apply the MPAM configuration to domains. Therefore, the MPAM config
should be applied to the domain at the boot time statically via
device tree properties.

This commit introduces device tree property "xen,domain-mpam-l3-cpbm"
to specify the MPAM cache portion bitmap of the domain L3 cache. The
value will be applied to corresponding MPAM registers at the boot time.

Signed-off-by: Henry Wang <Henry.Wang@arm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
Issue-Id: SCM-2794
---
 docs/misc/arm/device-tree/booting.txt | 9 +++++++++
 xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c           | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/misc/arm/device-tree/booting.txt b/docs/misc/arm/device-tree/booting.txt
index bbd955e9c2f6..733eed34114f 100644
--- a/docs/misc/arm/device-tree/booting.txt
+++ b/docs/misc/arm/device-tree/booting.txt
@@ -260,6 +260,15 @@ with the following properties:
     value specified by Xen command line parameter gnttab_max_maptrack_frames
     (or its default value if unspecified, i.e. 1024) is used.
 
+- xen,domain-mpam-l3-cpbm
+
+    Optional. A 32-bit integer specifying the MPAM cache portion
+    bitmap (CPBM) for the domain L3 cache. Note that MPAM has architecture
+    maximum 32-bit CPBM, but hardware may have different implementations.
+    If the CPBM value given in the device tree exceeds the maximum value
+    of the system, it will be clamped to the maximum value supported
+    by the system.
+
 Under the "xen,domain" compatible node, one or more sub-nodes are present
 for the DomU kernel and ramdisk.
 
diff --git a/xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c b/xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c
index 7937cc1bc930..ba20793f103d 100644
--- a/xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c
+++ b/xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c
@@ -3785,6 +3785,14 @@ void __init create_domUs(void)
 #endif
         }
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_MPAM
+        if ( mpam_enabled )
+        {
+            dt_property_read_u32(node, "xen,domain-mpam-l3-cpbm",
+                                 &d_cfg.arch.mpam.l3_cpbm);
+        }
+#endif
+
         /*
          * The variable max_init_domid is initialized with zero, so here it's
          * very important to use the pre-increment operator to call
-- 
